WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.303
-Our first guest tonight
is an Academy Award-nominated

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.538
actress you know from films
like "Little Women,"

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.973
"Black Widow," and "Midsommar."

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:10.109
She stars in "The Wonder,"
which is in select theaters now

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.045
and available on Netflix
November 16th.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:15.014
Please welcome back to the show
Florence Pugh, everybody!

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.849
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:24.757 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:32.698 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:35.802
So happy you're here.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.337
-Wow!
-You've done the show before,

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.971
but this is the first time
in person.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.306
And it's a nice,
lovely difference.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.708
-Yeah, but I did it
with slippers on.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.142
-You did it with slippers on.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.476
-That's very kind of you
to admit

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:45.645
that you were wearing slippers.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.046
I could tell something
was a little off.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.814
-Yeah.

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.150
-You've had a very busy year.
-I have.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.052
-And we talked last time
about how your grandparents

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.455
are very proud of you,
very involved in your life.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.323
And you brought --

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.859
you brought your grandmother
to a red carpet.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.128
This is the first time
she's red-carpeted with you?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.230
-This is the first time
she's red-carpeted.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.232
-And it was Venice.
So that's a pretty...

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.667
-It was huge.
-...considerable red carpet.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.502
-I've never been on a carpet
like that before.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.871
Maybe BAFTAs or Oscars.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.274
But Venice was so massive.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.843
And Gran came on
and got addicted to it.

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.879
Like, fully got addicted.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.914
-So would you say she --
Did she have any trepidation,

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.250
or did she immediately
find her way into it?

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.086
-Well it started because --
I mean, it's actually quite sad.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.255
She wasn't going to renew her
passport because she was like,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.524
"Well, I'm not going to travel
before I die."

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.326
And I was like,
"That is so bleak.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.661
And of course you are.

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.263
You're an adventurer.
We've got to do this."

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.598
So I said, "Well, Gran, like,

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.868
what about coming
to the premiere in Venice?

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.336
If you don't have a passport,

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.670
you're not going
to be able to come."

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.405
And so she renewed it
after that, because she said,

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.574
"Yes, I should come to Venice,"
and I was like, "Okay."

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.510
She came to Venice.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.178
And the plan wasn't to go
on the carpet.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.179
The plan was for her to come --
my family --

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:55.748
my whole family came.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.116
And as I finished the carpet,

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:00.386
I turned around, and my gran
was in front of all these

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.056
shouting photographers
just standing there.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.424
And I said,
"Do you want to come with me?"

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.360
And she goes,
"Oh, alright, then."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.661
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.963
So we march over
to the photographers.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.832
It's quite, like, aggressive
when you're out there.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.100
There's so many people
shouting, screaming,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.236
so many photographers
asking you to look here

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.638
and there and everywhere.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.707
And I take her on,
and I'm, like, looking at all

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.942
these photographers like,
"Be nice. Be really nice."

00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:25.645
And they do it.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.381
And I suddenly hear all these
people screaming from behind.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.683
And I thought they were being
really rude to Gran.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.652
So I was about to turn around
and, like, tell some people off.

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:35.220
And when I turned around,

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.925
the whole wall of photographers
behind me were all like,

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.960
"No, we want pictures!"

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.296
So my gran
then starts pirouetting

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:46.331
and, like, curtseying,
and it was amazing.

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:49.035
-I was wanted to say --
this is not the photo of a woman

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:52.371
who doesn't have a passport.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.207
This is a woman of the world.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.042
-Yeah.
-And anyone with a scarf

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.878
like that has to have
an active passport.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.179
-She's raving. She's raving.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:02.781
-Now, this is a thing I found --

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:04.283
Here's another lovely one.
Look at that.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:07.153
And I do feel like she's willing
to share the stage with you.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.821
It's very lovely how
she's willing to share with you.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.389
-I know, I know, and
I twirled her and everything.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:11.824
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.159
It's very dangerous
to twirl a grandparent, FYI.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.761
-And she said -- She goes,

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.697
"And I was wearing
my uncomfortable heels."

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:21.401
I was like, "Well done, Gran."
-Lesson learned.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.604
So, I found this, because, you
know, we were talking backstage.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.538
My parents are on the show
every year for Thanksgiving.

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:29.074
I thought I'd do it once,
and now there's no way
to take it away from them.

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:30.443
They're here every year.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.144
This has also happened
with Gran.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:35.548
Gran has now done
back-to-back carpets with you.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.316
Here she is
for your latest film.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.751
And so --
-Exactly.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.721
So I didn't -- When we finished
the premiere in Venice for

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.322
"Don't Worry Darling," I said,

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.357
"Granny, do you think
you might want to do it again?"

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:47.793
And she goes,
"I think I should."

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.228
I was like, "Okay."

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:54.066
But between both premieres,
she wasn't feeling very well.

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:55.634
And so I wasn't
going to push her.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.904
And when we got to that
premiere, I did the carpet

00:03:58.904 --> 00:04:01.441
and, you know,
all of the madness.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:05.778
And I turned to my right,
and again, in amongst --

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.713
In amongst
all the photographers,

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:09.682
she's standing there like this.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.850
And I turn to my publicist,
and my publicist goes...

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.053
[Whispering] "She wants
to get on the carpet."

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:18.190
So I go over, and Gran, again,
she's like, "I'm here!"

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.060
She loves it.
-I heard you call her Granzo.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.029
Is "Granzo" common or is that
just unique to your family?

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:25.831
-Granzo, Granzilla.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:27.299
-Okay. Got it.
-Granny...

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:29.902
-So you've got a lot of
different nicknames for her.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.404
-And now are you concerned
about, the next carpet,

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:34.373
she will have her own publicist?
Is that something you're...

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:38.244
-The last premiere, we went
to Ireland and we opened --

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.412
We did our premiere
there in Dublin.

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.715
When I got -- I sat in my seat,
and a fan came up to me

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:45.484
and said, "Is your granny here?"

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.886
And I said,
"No, she's not here."

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.989
She was like, "Oh.
Well, I made her something.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.891
I'm a designer,
and I made her a handbag."

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:55.227
So I take this present.
And I go, "For Gran?"

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:57.430
And she goes, "Yeah, for Gran."

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.999
So all night long it was going
through my whole team's hand.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.568
Like, "Make sure
this gets home to Gran."

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.336
So she's got fan gifts
and everything.

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:05.505
-I love it. As she should.

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:07.440
The whole world
has come around to a place

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.342
they should have been for years,
which is Gran's the one.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:12.611
-Exactly. Gran is the one.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.313
-Now, you obviously
grew up in England.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.514
Thanksgiving not a thing there.

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:18.083
-Yeah.
-You have come to adapt it?

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:20.052
Are you going to celebrate it
this year?

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:21.754
-Well, yeah, I am going to
celebrate it.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.390
I've done, for the last three
years, Thanksgiving.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.724
Yeah.
For the last two, I've cooked.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:27.559
This year,
I'm going to semi-cook.

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.395
-Okay. What is semi cook?
What are you going to take on?

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.030
-I'm not going to say
I'm cooking,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.099
but I'm going to be there
if anybody needs me with a pan.

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:36.068
-Oh, so that sounds like
not at all cooking.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.836
-That's like -- No.

00:05:37.836 --> 00:05:41.140
Oh, my God. That's like my dad
cooking in a kitchen.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.375
"I'm not cooking, but I'm
definitely going to take over."

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.579
-It is a very -- The stakes are
high with a Thanksgiving dinner.

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.114
-Yeah.
-How do you feel --

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.682
How would you grade yourself
the last few years you did it?

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:50.983
-I put a bit of a twist on it.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.252
I don't do all
the bits and bobs.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:56.088
Why is there sweet potatoes
and marshmallows? That's weird.

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.457
-No, it's awful.
Yeah. A lot of it's awful.

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.793
-Why are there sweeties
in your food, guys?

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.228
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:05.531
-There's some terrible mistakes
we made years ago,

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:09.335
and now we're living with them.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.170
Out of the chains of tradition.
I think that's the thing.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.371
-Okay.
-So it's very smart of you.

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.574
But you cooked the full turkey?

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.975
-Well, n-- Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.843
So it sounds like
maybe you just made dinner.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:20.045
-No, I make a really good roast,
actually.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:21.113
-Okay, there you go.

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.182
-I just don't do
all the bits and bobs.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:26.184
-Alright.
-I actually last year --

00:06:26.184 --> 00:06:27.720
Because it all failed.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.188
Like, the family...had COVID,

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.822
so I had to start doing
two roast chickens,

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:33.092
which wasn't that bad,
but there was no turkey left.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.428
-Alright. I'm not complaining.
I give you full credit.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.196
I also want to talk about
this wonderful film.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.031
So you're going to stick around.
Is that alright?

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.399
-But what about
your Thanksgiving?

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.268
We didn't even talk
about your Thanksgiving.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.102
-It's all done and ready.
I already cooked it.

00:06:44.102 --> 00:06:45.637
-Really?!
-It's ready to go.

00:06:45.637 --> 00:06:48.073
-Is it in the freezer?
-No, it's not in the freezer.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:51.210
I have it at very low heat
in the oven.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.178
I have it at 5 --
You keep it at 5 degrees.

00:06:53.178 --> 00:06:55.080
You cook it
a month ahead of time

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.582
then just keep it at 5 degrees.
-It's going to be,

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.485
like, dry, like,
astronaut food by the end.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.887
-You have to ladle gravy
over it every 15 minutes.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.856
We're going to take
a commercial break,

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.991
and I'm going to
run and ladle it,

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.960
and then I'll come back
and we'll talk.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.530
We'll be right back with more
from Florence Pugh!

